<DemoExample Title="Width" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" Id="example8" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>FitWidth</b> shrinks the navbar to the width of its own content, and <b>FullWidth</b> stretches it
        over the full width of its container. Without either one the navbar takes the width its container
        gives it. Those two size the bar; <b>Justified</b> sizes the options inside it, giving each one an
        equal share instead of the width of its own label, which is how a navigation bar keeps its
        destinations on a predictable grid, and <b>Scrollable</b> is the other answer to a bar that
        runs out of room: it leaves the options at the size of their own content and scrolls them instead.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>FitWidth:</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarOption" FitWidth>
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Home" IconName="@BitIconName.Home" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Products" IconName="@BitIconName.ProductVariant" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Academy" IconName="@BitIconName.LearningTools" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Profile" IconName="@BitIconName.Contact" />
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div>FullWidth:</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarOption" FullWidth>
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Home" IconName="@BitIconName.Home" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Products" IconName="@BitIconName.ProductVariant" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Academy" IconName="@BitIconName.LearningTools" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Profile" IconName="@BitIconName.Contact" />
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div>Justified (options of unequal label length):</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarOption" Justified>
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Home" IconName="@BitIconName.Home" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Products &amp; services" IconName="@BitIconName.ProductVariant" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Academy" IconName="@BitIconName.LearningTools" />
            <BitNavBarOption Text="Me" IconName="@BitIconName.Contact" />
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Alignment" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" Id="example9" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
